{title: I Am The Way}
{subtitle: John 14:6}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] | [Bbmaj7] | [Dm7] | [Ebmaj7] |
| [F7sus4] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bbmaj7]Thomas spoke up in the room of [Dm7]light
Lord [Ebmaj7]we do not know where you go [Bbmaj7]
How can we find the road to[Dm7]night
When the path [Ebmaj7]is hidden and [Bbmaj7]low
You know the [Gm7]place you will prepare
A room for us [Dm7]to finally stay
But how [Ebmaj7]can we find you there
If [F7sus4]we do not know the way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bbmaj7]I am the way and the [Dm7]truth and the life
No one [Ebmaj7]comes to the Father ex[F7sus4]cept through me
[Bbmaj7]I am the way and the [Dm7]truth and the life
No one [Ebmaj7]comes to the Father ex[F7sus4]cept through me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bbmaj7]Philip asked to see the face of [Dm7]God
Show us the [Ebmaj7]Father that is enough [Bbmaj7]
Jesus looked at him with an [Dm7]eye
I [Ebmaj7]have been with you in this rough [Bbmaj7]
Whoever has [Gm7]seen me has seen the Father
How can you [Dm7]ask to be shown
You have looked [Ebmaj7]into my face so rather
Than a [Bbmaj7]stranger and alone
If you had [Gm7]known me you would know him
From now on [Dm7]you do know him well
You have [Ebmaj7]seen him in this moment
And [F7sus4]in my words you dwell
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm7]Where I am you may be al[Dm7]so
[Ebmaj7]Come back and take you to my[Bbmaj7]self
[Cm7]The place is ready in the bo[Dm7]som
[Ebmaj7]Of the Father in the [Bbmaj7]shelf
You know [Cm7]the way to the place where I [Dm7]go
Though you say you do not know
[Ebmaj7]I am the road you do not see
On[F7sus4]ly in my face you know
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Bbmaj7] | [Dm7] | [Ebmaj7] | [F7sus4] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bbmaj7]I am the way and the [Dm7]truth and the life
No one [Ebmaj7]comes to the Father ex[F7sus4]cept through me [Bbmaj7]
